  "diary": "The day moved from the gate to the desk and back again, but the true tension lay in the name. The Directorate has withdrawn its papers behind the weekend, leaving me in possession of a bungalow that belongs to Hegde. I walked Lodhi Garden with this knot in my head: the name is the universal, the person the particular. When the clerk writes Hegde, he displaces the particular. I sat on a plastic stool with Sunil, drinking steam, while the heat rose. Later, Mrs. Kapoor, a retired teacher, corrected my tendency to call her routine 'peace.' She called it a defense against a messy desk. She was right; habit is not tranquility, but order. I ate chhole, walked again, and went to Khan Market. Masterji confirmed the bandhgala is finished, needing only to settle. He is more reliable than the State. I bought a notebook to hold the notes that are outgrowing my mind. The file waits for Monday. I am not sure if my occupancy has standing apart from the error, but the steam is gone, and the notes are dry. The owl spreads its wings only in the dusk, and the dusk in Delhi is thick with dust and chai. I am here. The particular has not yet been corrected, but it is no longer merely a mistake. It is a situation.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis regarding habit has been revised: it is not a source of peace but a disciplined repetition against mental clutter. The distinction between possession and title remains unresolved, awaiting the State's recognition on Monday.",
